# NetEpic rulebook source of truth

Baguettepic is a companion app for Palladium NetEpic 3. Game rules, army books, and LaTeX source live in a **separate** repository — not in a local Palladium folder on disk.

## Canonical repo

- Repository: https://github.com/Phusck/NetEpicFR300-EnglishTranslation
- Default branch: `Development`
- Do **not** assume a local path such as `Palladium NetEpic 3 English Latex/…`

## Important folders

| Content | Path in that repo |
|---|---|
| Core rulebook (LaTeX) | `Rulebook 303/` |
| Tyranids army book | `Tyranids 300/` |
| Domain class diagram (schema inspiration) | `Rulebook 303/class-diagram.md` |

Key rulebook sections under `Rulebook 303/`:

- `00 - Intro/` — Important Concepts, Introduction, Preparing for Battle
- `01 - Game Turn/` — Strategy, Movement, Combat, End phases
- `02 - Something/` — Morale, Terrain, Titans and Praetorians
- `03 - Special Abilities/`
- `04 - Markers and Templates/`
- `main.tex` / `Preamble.tex` — document entry points

## Agent behavior

- When seeding or editing `Database/*.sql`, special abilities, or in-app rule text, read the matching `.tex` (or diagram) from the GitHub repo above.
- Prefer fetching from that repo (`gh api`, clone, or raw GitHub URLs on branch `Development`) over inventing rules.
- Cite source paths relative to that repo (e.g. `Rulebook 303/01 - Game Turn/Combat Phase.tex`, `Tyranids 300/Unit Profiles.tex`).
- Keep long rule prose out of Cursor rules; point at the files instead.
- This app repo (`Baguettepic`) owns the MAUI client and MySQL seed/schema; the translation repo owns the printed-rules source.
